---
permalink: "/apps/orbit/"
layout: cosmique.njk
# Orbit hasn't shipped. While this is true the page is a coming-soon stub: the
# launch page below (features, screenshots, formats, pricing) is kept intact in
# the else branch untouched. Flip to false at launch to bring all of it back.
comingSoon: true
eleventyComputed:
  pageTitle: "{% if comingSoon %}Orbit — Coming soon{% else %}Orbit — The music server built for serious collectors{% endif %}"
  pageDescription: "{% if comingSoon %}Orbit is a self-hosted music server for serious collectors, in development at Cosmique.{% else %}Self-hosted music server with native apps for iPhone, iPad, Mac, Apple Watch, Apple TV and CarPlay. Bit-perfect playback, vinyl-grade metadata, classical structure.{% endif %}"
---

<div class="wrap">

  <!-- Header -->
  <header class="ds-header">
    <div class="brand">
      <a href="{{ '/' | url }}">COSMIQUE</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <b>ORBIT</b>
    </div>
    <nav class="nav">
      {%- if not comingSoon %}
      <a href="#features">Features</a>
      <a href="#formats">Formats</a>
      <a href="#pricing">Pricing</a>
      {%- endif %}
      <a href="{{ '/apps/orbit/support/' | url }}">Support</a>
    </nav>
    <button class="theme-toggle" aria-label="Toggle dark mode">◐</button>
  </header>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="o2-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Self-hosted music system</p>
    <h1 class="h1">The music server built<br>for serious collectors.</h1>
    <p class="lead o2-hero-lead">
      A server that runs on your hardware. Native apps for iPhone, iPad, Mac,
      Apple&nbsp;Watch, Apple&nbsp;TV and CarPlay. For people who can hear the difference
      between pressings — and want a server that can too.
    </p>
    {% if comingSoon %}
    <div class="o2-cta">
      <span class="chip"><span class="dot"></span>In development — coming soon</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  {% else %}
    <div class="o2-cta">
      <a class="btn" href="#pricing">See pricing</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="{{ '/apps/orbit/support/' | url }}">Get started →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="o2-chips">
      <span class="chip"><span class="dot"></span>Server · Docker / Linux / macOS</span>
      <span class="chip"><span class="dot"></span>Apps · iPhone / iPad / Mac / Watch / TV / CarPlay</span>
    </div>

    <figure class="macwin o2-hero-shot">
      <div class="bar"><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/hero-player-cinematic.webp' | url }}"
             alt="Orbit's Mac app playing a 1978 German pressing of Kraftwerk — Die Mensch·Maschine, with label, catalog number, condition and playback equipment in the side rail"
             width="2000" height="1242">
      </div>
    </figure>
    <p class="o2-caption mono">THE MAC PLAYER — PRESSING DETAILS AND THE EQUIPMENT BEHIND THE RIP, WHERE THEY BELONG.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- 01 Versions -->
  <section class="o2-feature" id="features">
    <div class="o2-feature-text">
      <p class="kick">01 — Versions</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Every pressing tells a different story</h2>
      <p>
        Most servers see one album. Orbit sees your 1978 Kling&nbsp;Klang original and the
        2020 remaster as what they are: different records. Keep every version, switch
        between them with one click, and mark the one that sounds best — with a note
        that says why.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="macwin">
      <div class="bar"><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/mac-album-versions.webp' | url }}"
             alt="Album page with two switchable pressings of Die Mensch·Maschine — German 1978 and European 2020"
             loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1117">
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- 02 Vinyl -->
  <section class="o2-feature o2-feature-reverse">
    <div class="o2-feature-text">
      <p class="kick">02 — Vinyl</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Vinyl is a first-class citizen</h2>
      <p>
        Label, catalog number, matrix etching, condition grade — and the turntable and
        cartridge that made the rip. Orbit keeps the full provenance of every record,
        down to DSD128 needle-drops that play on every device you own.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="o2-pair">
      <figure class="device--iphone">
        <div class="screen">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/ios-vinyl-equipment.webp' | url }}"
               alt="iPhone showing vinyl specifications, pressing information, condition and digitization equipment"
               loading="lazy" width="900" height="1956">
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="macwin">
        <div class="bar"><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
        <div class="viewport">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/mac-album-dsd.webp' | url }}"
               alt="Ghost — Prequelle as a DSD128 vinyl rip with side-numbered tracks"
               loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1117">
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 Classical -->
  <section class="o2-feature">
    <div class="o2-feature-text">
      <p class="kick">03 — Classical</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Classical, done properly</h2>
      <p>
        Composer → Work → Movement — not “Track 7”. Opera acts and scenes, conductors,
        orchestras and soloists, with authoritative catalog data from OpenOpus.
        Your Beethoven shelf finally makes sense.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="browser">
      <div class="bar">
        <div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <div class="addr">orbit.local/composers</div>
      </div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/web-composers.webp' | url }}"
             alt="Composer browser listing Bach, Beethoven and others with period and lifespan"
             loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1125">
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 Playback -->
  <section class="o2-feature o2-feature-reverse">
    <div class="o2-feature-text">
      <p class="kick">04 — Playback</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Bit-perfect, to the last bit</h2>
      <p>
        Exclusive mode hands your USB DAC to Orbit and nobody else: no system mixer,
        no resampling, automatic sample-rate switching, DSD. Gapless playback and
        loudness analysis come standard — and effective-bit-depth checks call out
        fake hi-res before you shelve it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="macwin">
      <div class="bar"><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/mac-player-radar.webp' | url }}"
             alt="Radar player layout with sonic dimensions and the full signal chain: format, pressing, condition, equipment"
             loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1117">
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- 05 Everywhere -->
  <section class="o2-feature">
    <div class="o2-feature-text">
      <p class="kick">05 — Everywhere</p>
      <h2 class="h2">Everywhere you listen</h2>
      <p>
        Native on every Apple screen. Download albums for offline. Away from home, your
        library follows you through an end-to-end encrypted relay — your server stays
        private, your music doesn’t stop.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="o2-pair o2-pair-phones">
      <figure class="device--iphone">
        <div class="screen">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/ios-player-oxygene.webp' | url }}"
               alt="iPhone player: Jean-Michel Jarre — Oxygène in FLAC 24-bit / 96 kHz"
               loading="lazy" width="900" height="1956">
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="device--iphone">
        <div class="screen">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/ios-editorial.webp' | url }}"
               alt="Editorial mode: the library as a magazine, with featured albums and liner notes"
               loading="lazy" width="900" height="1956">
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OSP callout -->
  <div class="callout o2-callout">
    <span class="dot"></span>
    <p>Multiroom zones today. <strong>OSP</strong> — our bit-perfect, sub-millisecond
    multiroom streaming protocol — coming soon.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 06 Collection -->
  <section class="o2-collection">
    <p class="kick o2-kick-center">06 — Your collection</p>
    <h2 class="h2">A collection you can see</h2>
    <p class="o2-collection-lede">
      Groove and Spine map your library by era, intensity and sound.
      Crate-digging, without the dust.
    </p>
    <div class="o2-pair o2-pair-phones o2-pair-center">
      <figure class="device--iphone">
        <div class="screen">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/ios-collection-groove.webp' | url }}"
               alt="Groove view: albums plotted by year and intensity" loading="lazy" width="900" height="1956">
        </div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="device--iphone">
        <div class="screen">
          <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/ios-collection-spine.webp' | url }}"
               alt="Spine view: albums as vinyl discs on a decade timeline" loading="lazy" width="900" height="1956">
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<!-- Dark interlude — token-driven dark subtree -->
<section class="o2-dark" data-theme="dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <figure class="macwin">
      <div class="bar"><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div></div>
      <div class="viewport">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/orbit/mac-player-cinematic-dark.webp' | url }}"
             alt="The Cinematic player in dark mode with true black background"
             loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1170">
      </div>
    </figure>
    <p class="o2-caption mono">DARK MODE, WITH TRUE BLACK FOR OLED. YOUR LISTENING ROOM, UNDISTURBED.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">

  <!-- Formats -->
  <section class="o2-formats" id="formats">
    <p class="kick">07 — Formats</p>
    <h2 class="h2">If you can collect it, Orbit can play it</h2>
    <table class="o2-format-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Lossless</th>
          <td>FLAC · ALAC · WAV · AIFF · APE · WavPack</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Hi-res &amp; DSD</th>
          <td>DSF / DFF (DSD64–DSD256) · SACD ISO extraction · up to 384 kHz / 32-bit</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Lossy</th>
          <td>MP3 · AAC · OGG Vorbis · Opus</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">And the rest</th>
          <td>CUE sheets · multi-disc sets · on-the-fly transcoding for the road</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing -->
  <section class="o2-pricing" id="pricing">
    <p class="kick">08 — Pricing</p>
    <h2 class="h2">Free at home. Pro everywhere else.</h2>
    <p class="o2-pricing-lede">
      The server and every app are free on your home network. Orbit&nbsp;Pro unlocks the
      rest — one subscription, every Apple device, Family Sharing included.
    </p>
    <div class="tiers">
      <div class="tier">
        <div class="name">Free</div>
        <div class="price free">$0</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Self-hosted server, full library management</li>
          <li>Every native app</li>
          <li>Playback on your home network</li>
          <li>No account required</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <div class="name">Orbit Pro · Monthly</div>
        <div class="price">$2.99<small> / month</small></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Bit-perfect exclusive mode</li>
          <li>Gapless · crossfade · loudness normalization</li>
          <li>Offline downloads &amp; remote listening</li>
          <li>Multi-zone &amp; multi-server</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="tier feature-tier">
        <div class="name">Orbit Pro · Annual</div>
        <div class="price">$24<small> / year</small></div>
        <ul>
          <li>Everything in Pro</li>
          <li>7-day free trial</li>
          <li>Two months free vs monthly</li>
          <li>Family Sharing</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="o2-pricing-note">
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="{{ '/apps/orbit/pricing/' | url }}">Full pricing &amp; FAQ →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="ds-footer">
    <div class="brand"><a href="{{ '/' | url }}">COSMIQUE</a> <span>/</span> <b>ORBIT</b></div>
    <div class="links">
      {%- if not comingSoon %}
      <a href="{{ '/apps/orbit/pricing/' | url }}">Pricing</a>
      {%- endif %}
      <a href="{{ '/apps/orbit/support/' | url }}">Support</a>
      <a href="{{ '/apps/orbit/privacy/' | url }}">Privacy</a>
      <a href="{{ '/apps/orbit/terms/' | url }}">Terms</a>
      <a href="mailto:hello@cosmique.io">hello@cosmique.io</a>
    </div>
  </footer>

</div>
